of visible light emitted by a light source.',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(853,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','LUX','Lux','The International System unit of illumination, equal to one lumen per square meter.',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(854,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','M57','Mile Per Minute ','The number of mile per minute the trade item or part of the trade item moves.',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(855,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','M58','Mile Per Second ','The number of mile per second the trade item or part of the trade item moves.',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(856,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','M60','Metre Per Hour','The number of meter per hour the trade item or part of the trade item moves.',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(857,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','M62','Kilometre Per Second ','The number of kilometre per second the trade item or part of the trade item moves.',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(858,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','M63','Inch Per Minute','The number of inch per minute the trade item or part of the trade item moves.',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(859,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','M64','Yard Per Second','The number of yard per second the trade item or part of the trade item moves.',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(860,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','M65','Yard Per Minute','The number of yard per minute the trade item or part of the trade item moves.',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(861,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','M66','Yard Per Hour','The number of yard per hour the trade item or part of the trade item moves.',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(862,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','MAW','Megawatt','A unit of power defining the rate of energy transferred or consumed when a current of 1000 amperes flows due to a potential of 1000 volts at unity power factor.',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(863,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','MBR','Millibar','Millibar- a hundred pascals (10 to the 2nd power)',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(864,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','MC','Microgram','A microgram is one millionth of a gram (0.000001)',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(865,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','MEQ','Milliequivalents','mEq or milliequivalents, the measure is used in terms of milliequivalents of solute per liter of solvent (or milliNormal where mEq/L = mN). This is especially common for measurement of compounds in biological fluids; for instance, the healthy level of potassium in the blood of a human is defined between 3.5 and 5.0 mEq/L. To better be able to denote the units of measure for nutrients as used in business today.',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(866,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','MGM','Milligram','A milligram is one thousandth of a gram (0.001)',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(867,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','MHZ','Megahertz','A unit of frenquecy equal to 106 Hertz',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(868,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','MIK','Square mile','A square mile is an area of a square whose sides are exactly 1 mile in length.',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(869,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','MIN','Minute (unit of time)','A minute is a unit of time equal to 1/60th of an hour or 60 seconds',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(870,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','MIU','Million International Unit (NIE)','A unit of count defining the number of international units in multiples of 106.',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(871,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','MLT','Millilitre','A millilitre is one thousandth of a litre (0.001)',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(872,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','MMK','Square millimetre','A square millimetre is an area of a square whose sides are exactly 1 millimetre in',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(873,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','MMQ','Cubic millimetre','A cubic millimetre is the volume of a cube of side length one milliimetre (0.001 m)',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(874,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','MMT','Millimetre','A millimetre is one thousandth of a metre (0.001)',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(875,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','MON','Month','Unit of time equal to 1/12 of a year of 365,25 days',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(876,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','MPN','Most Probable Number ','Most Probable Number: is a method of getting quantitative data on concentrations of discrete items from positive/negative (incidence) data.. ',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(877,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','MQH','Cubic Metre Per Hour','Cubic Metre Per Hour',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(878,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','MTK','Square metre','A square metre is an area of a square whose sides are exactly 1 metre in length.',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(879,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','MTQ','Cubic metre','A cubic metre is the volume of a cube of side length one metre.',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(880,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','MTR','Metre','The metre is the basic unit of length in the International System of Units (SI).',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(881,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','MTS','Metre Per Second','Defines the speed defined by distance in metres divided by time in seconds.',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(882,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','MWH','Megawatt hour (1000 kW.h)','A unit of energy defining the total amount of bulk energy transferred or consumed.',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(883,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','NA','Milligram per Kilogram (mg/kg)','Milligram per Kilogram (mg/kg)',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(884,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','NCL','Number of cells','Number of cells',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(885,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','NEW','Newton','Newton',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(886,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','NIU','Number of International Units','A unit of count defining the number of international units. The International Unit is a unit of measurement for the amount of a substance, based on measured biological activity or effect.The unit is used for vitamins, hormones, some medications, vaccines, blood products, and similar biologically active substances',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(887,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','NPR','Number of pairs','Number of pairs',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(888,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','NU','Newton Metre','Newton Metre',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(889,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','OHM','Ohm','A unit for electrical impedance, the ratio of the voltage phasor to the electric current phasor.',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(890,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','ON','Ounces per square yard','The weight of one square yard of the material expressed in ounces. Commonly used to express the density or weight of all types of paper, paperboard, and fabric, e.g. 20 OZ or 20 Weight denim has an area density of 20 oz/yd2.The term density here is used somewhat incorrectly, as density is mass by volume. More precisely, it is a measure of the area density, areal density, or surface density.',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(891,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','ONZ','Ounce','A unit of mass with several definitions, the most commonly used of which are equal to approximately 30 grams',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(892,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','OPM','Oscillations Per Minute ','Oscillations Per Minute ',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(893,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','OZA','Fluid ounce (US)','A fluid ounce (US) is equal to one sixteenth (1/16) of a US pint or 29.5735295625 millilitres .',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(894,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','OZI','Fluid ounce (UK)','A fluid ounce (UK) is equal to one thirtieth (1/30) of a UK pint or 28.4130625 millilitres.',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(895,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','P1','Percent','A unit of proportion equal to 0.01.',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(896,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','PAL','Pascal','The pascal (symbol: Pa) is the SI derived unit of pressure, stress, Young\'s modulus and tensile strength. It is a measure of force per unit area, defined as one newton per square metre.',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(897,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','PD','Pad','A unit of count defining the number of pads (pad: block of paper sheets fastened together at one end).',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(898,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','PFU','Plaque Forming unit(s)','Plaque Forming unit(s)',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(899,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','PNT','Point','A single unit on a scale of measurement as part of an incentive program or pricing structure used as a means of making a quantitative evaluation.',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(900,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','PR','Pair','A unit of count defining the number of pairs (pair: item described by two\'s).',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(901,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','PRS','Potential Renal Solute Load','Potential Renal Solute Load',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(902,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','PS','Pound-force per square inch','The pound-force per square inch (symbol: psi or lbf/in2 or lbf/in2) is a unit of pressure or of stress based on avoirdupois units. It is the pressure resulting from a force of one pound-force applied to an area of one square inch. Other abbreviations are used that append a modifier to \"psi\". However, the US National Institute of Standards and Technology recommends that, to avoid confusion, any modifiers be instead applied to the quantity being measured rather than the unit of measure[1] For example, \"Pg = 100 psi\" rather than \"P = 100 psig\".',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(903,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','PTD','Dry Pint (US)','The United States dry pint is equal one eighth of a US dry gallon or one half US dry quarts. It is used in the United States but is not as common as the liquid pint.',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(904,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','PTI','Pint (UK)','A pint (UK) is equal to 1/8 Gallon (UK); used primarly as a measure for beer and cider when sold by the glass.',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(905,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','PTL','Liquid pint (US)','The US liquid pint is equal one eighth of a United States liquid gallon.',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(906,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','PTN','Portion','Portion',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(907,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','Q30','pH (potential of Hydrogen)',' The activity of the (solvated) hydrogen ion (a logarithmic measure used to state the acidity or alkalinity of a chemical solution).',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(908,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','Q32','Femtolitre','Femtolitre- Femtolitre is the metric unit of volume equal to one thousand trillionth (European) or one quadrillionth (American) litre. One femtolitre is the same as one cubic micrometre (μm3), which can be represented numerically as 0.00000000000001/liter. ',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(909,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','Q33',' Picolitre',' Picolitre- Picoliter is the metric unit of volume equal to a trillionth (one millionth of a millionth) of a liter, which can be represented numerically as 0.000000000001/liter. just as the prefix nano denotes a billionth part. ',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(910,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','Q34','Nanolitre','Nanolitre- Nanolitre is the metric unit of volume equal to one billionth of a litre, which can be represented numerically as 0.000000001/liter. ',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(911,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','QB','Page - hardcopy','A unit of count defining the number of hardcopy pages (hardcopy page: a page rendered as printed or written output on paper, film, or other permanent medium).',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(912,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','QTD','Quart (US dry)','A US dry quart is equal to 1/32 of a US bushel, exactly 1.101220942715 litres.',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(913,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','QTL','Liquid quart (US)','A US liquid quart exactly equals 57.75 cubic inches, which is exactly equal to 0.946352946 litres.',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(914,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','R9','Thousand cubic metre','Thousand cubic metre',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(915,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','RPM','Revolutions Per Minute','Revolutions Per Minute',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(916,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','S4','Square Metre / Second','Metre squared per second.',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(917,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','SEC','Second (unit of time)','A second is a unit of time equal to 1/60th of an minute.',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(918,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','SET','Set','A unit of count defining the number of sets (set: a number of objects grouped together).',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(919,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','SMI','Mile (statute mile)','A statute mile of 5,280 feet (exactly 1,609.344 meters).',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(920,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','SQE','SQ-E','Number of allergens based on the SQ-E unit',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(921,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','STN','Ton (US) or short ton (UK)','Ton (US) = 2000 Lb or 907 Kg',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(922,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','SX','Shipment','A unit of count defining the number of shipments (shipment: an amount of goods shipped or transported).',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(923,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','T3','Thousand piece','Thousand piece',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(924,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','TNE','Tonne','Metric ton = 1000 Kg',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(925,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','TPI','Teeth Per Inch','Teeth Per Inch',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(926,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','U2','Tablet','A unit of count defining the number of tablets (tablet: a small flat or compressed solid object).',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(927,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','UA','Torr','Torr',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(928,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','VLT','Volt','Volt',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(929,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','WEE','Week','A week is a time unit equal to seven days.',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(930,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','WHR','Watt hour','The watt-hour is a unit of energy equivalent to one watt of power expended for one hour of time; it is equal to 3.6 kilojoules. The watt-hour is rarely used to express energy in any form other than electrical.',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(931,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','WTT','Watt','A watt is a derived unit of power; one watt is equivalent to 1 joule (J) of energy per second.',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(932,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','X_CCA','Cold Cramp Amp','A measurement of the number of amps a battery can deliver at 0 ° F for 30 seconds and not drop below 7.2 volts.',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(933,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','X_CFG','Colony Forming Units per gram (CFU/g)\n','Colony Forming Units per gram (CFU/g). See CFU for definition of Colony Forming Unit',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(934,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','X_CFP','Colony Forming Units per Pound (CFU/lb)','Colony Forming Units per Pound (CFU/lb) See CFU for definition of Colony Forming Unit',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(935,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','X_CHD','Centisimal Hahnemannian Dilution (CH)','A count of attenuation steps or dilution levels representing the homeopathic potency of a substance using the Hahnemannian (CH) method of attenuation; commonly denoted as CH1, CH2, CH3, etc. Each centesimal attenuation step represents one part source material combined with 99 parts dilution medium; commonly denoted as C1, C2, C3, etc.',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(936,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','X_DBA','Decibar','Decibar',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(937,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','X_DWT','Penny Weight','A pennyweight (abbreviated dwt or denarius weight) is a unit of mass that is equal to 24 grains, 1⁄20 of a troy ounce, 1⁄240 of a troy pound, and exactly 1.55517384 grams. (Usage- The pennyweight is the common weight used in the valuation and measurement of precious metals. Jewellers use the pennyweight in calculating the amount and cost of precious metals used in fabricating or casting jewellery. Similarly, dentists and dental labs still use the pennyweight as the measure of precious metals in dental crowns and inlays.)',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(938,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','X_IUK','International Units per Kilogram (IU/kg)','International Units per Kilogram (IU/kg) a unit of activity or potency for vitamins, hormones, or other substances, defined individually for each substance in terms of the activity of a standard quantity or preparation.',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(939,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','X_KVN','Korsakovian (K)','A count of attenuation steps or dilution levels representing the homeopathic potency of a substance using the Korsakovian (K) method of attenuation; commonly denoted as CK1, CK2, CK3, etc.Each centesimal attenuation step represents one part source material combined with 99 parts dilution medium; commonly denoted as C1, C2, C3, etc.',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(940,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','X_MLM','Millesimai (LM)','A count of attenuation steps or dilution levels representing the homeopathic potency of a substance where each attenuation step represents one part source material combined with 49,999 parts dilution medium; commonly denoted as LM1, LM2, LM3, etc.',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(941,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','X_MPG','Miles Per Gallon','Fuel usage by the number of miles the trade item can go on 1 US gallon of fuel.',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(942,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','X_MTC','Mother tincture (Dry material)','A count of a dry crud medical substance Mother tincture, when used for homeopathic preparations, are liquid preparations obtained by the solvent action of a suitable vehicle upon raw materials. The raw materials (medical substance) are usually in the fresh form but may be dried. Mother tinctures for homeopathic preparations may also be obtained from plant juices, with, or without the addition of a vehicle.',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(943,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','X_NGM','Nanogram','A nano gram is 10-9 gram or a billionth of a gram..',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(944,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','X_PPC','Pixel per centimetre','A unit of count defining the number of pixels per linear centimetre as a measurement of the resolution of devices in various contexts; typically computer displays, image scanners or digital camera image sensors.',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(945,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','X_PPI','Pixel per inch','A unit of count defining the number of pixels per linear inch (PPI) as a measurement of the resolution of devices in various contexts; typically computer displays, image scanners or digital camera image sensors.',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(946,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','X_RAE','Retinol Activity Equivalents','A measure of vitamin A activity based on the capacity of the body to convert provitamin carotenoids containing at least one unsubstituted ionone ring to retinaldehyde. \n1 microgram RAE = 1 mg retinol = 12 mg β-carotene = 24 mg other vitamin A precursor carotenoids.\n\n',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(947,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','X_SIN','Thirty Seconds of an Inch','Thirty Seconds of an inch (1/32 or 0.3125). (Usage when measuring using some measuring tapes. Commonly used in model making and some hobbies for scaling to full size.  Also used in railway applications.)\n',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(948,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','X_SPS','Sample per second','A unit of count defining the number of samplings takes during a period of time',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(949,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','X_UIN','Ten Thousandths of an Inch','One Ten Thousandths of an inch or 0.0001 often called a \"tenth\" in machinery. (Usage- Measurements of some machine parts, gaps in spark plugs).',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(950,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','XRE','Retinol Equivalent (RE)','A unit used for quantifying the vitamin A value of sources of vitamin A, including both preformed retinoids and precursor carotenoids.  Examples include:\n. One RE is equivalent to 1 mcg of retinol, 6 mcg of Beta-carotene, or 12 mcg of other pro-vitamin A carotenoids.\n. One RE is equivalent to  0.3 International Units of retinol or 0.1 International Units of Beta-carotene.',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(951,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','XRO','Roll','A unit of count defining the number of rolls” where “Roll” is the name of the code value in UN/ECE Recommendation 21, pluralized as appropriate. ',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(952,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','XST','Sheet','A unit of count defining the number of “Sheets” where “Sheet” is the name of the code value in UN/ECE Recommendation 21, pluralized as appropriate.',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(953,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','YDK','Square Yard','A square yard is the area of a square with sides of one yard (three feet, thirty-six inches, 0.9144 metres) in length',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(954,1,'GDSNMeasurementUnitCode','YRD','Yard','A yard is equal to 3 feet or 36 inches or 0.9144 meter.',NULL,'7',1,'gdsnmeasurementunitcode'),(955,1,'PlatformTypeCode','10','Pallet 800 X 600 mm','Half size flat pallet with dimensions of 800 x 600 mm. also known as ISO 0 Pallet, 1/2 EUR Pallet, EUR 6 Pallet',NULL,'1',1,'platformtypecode'),(956,1,'PlatformTypeCode','11','Pallet 800 X 1200 mm','Flat pallet with dimensions of 800 x 1200 mm  ISO 6780 ISO 1 Pallet, EUR Pallet',NULL,'1',1,'platformtypecode'),(957,1,'PlatformTypeCode','12','Pallet 1200 X 1000 mm','Flat pallet with dimensions of 1200 x 1000 mm  ISO 6780 ISO 2 Pallet, EUR 2 Pallet',NULL,'1',1,'platformtypecode'),(958,1,'PlatformTypeCode','13','Pallet 600 X 400 mm','Quarter size of the standard EuroPallet with dimensions of 600 x 400 mm, Quarter size of the standard EuroPallet (EUR).',NULL,'1',1,'platformtypecode'),(959,1,'PlatformTypeCode','14','Pallet 400 X 300 mm','Eighth size of the standard EuroPallet (EUR) with dimensions of 400 x 300 mm. 1/8 EUR Pallet.',NULL,'1',1,'platformtypecode'),(960,1,'PlatformTypeCode','25','Australian Pallet','Standardised square pallet with dimensions of 1165 x 1165 mm, which perfectly fits in the RACE container of the Australian Railway.',NULL,'1',1,'platformtypecode'),(961,1,'PlatformTypeCode','27','Unspecified','Platform of Unspecified Weight or Dimension: Pallet level hierarchy is being shipped on a shipping platform of unknown dimensions or unknown weight. The platform weight or dimension may differ within the same shipment. All other values including null would indicate that the weight and dimensions include the shipping platform.',NULL,'1',1,'platformtypecode'),(962,1,'PlatformTypeCode','31','Pallet 1000 X 600 mm','Half size flat pallet with dimensions of 1000 x 600 mm. 1/2 ISO 2 Pallet.',NULL,'1',1,'platformtypecode'),(963,1,'PlatformTypeCode','32','Block Pallet','A pallet constructed with blocks at the corners and middle to which three stringers boards are attached with top deck boards attached perpendicular to the stringers. Block pallets can have a variety of bottom deck configurations; no bottom boards, boards parallel to the top deck boards or a full parameter base similar to a picture frame.',NULL,'1',1,'platformtypecode'),(964,1,'PlatformTypeCode','33','Dolly','A portable, horizontal, rigid platform on wheels or rollers, used as a base for assembling, storing, stacking, handling and transporting goods as a unit, suitable for manually positioning.',NULL,'1',1,'platformtypecode'),(965,1,'PlatformTypeCode','35','Pallet 1000 X 1200 mm','Standard EuroPallet (EUR3) size with dimensions of 1000 x 1200 mm. EUR 3 Pallet',NULL,'1',1,'platformtypecode'),(966,1,'PlatformTypeCode','38','Horizontal Drum Pallet','A rigid platform with integrated restraints to prevent horizontally orientated cylindrical containers from slipping.\nHorizontal Drum Pallets are used for assembling, storing, stacking, handling and transporting cylindrical containers, e.g. drums, barrels, or kegs, as a unit load, suitable for lifting by a forklift, pallet jack, or other jacking device.',NULL,'1',1,'platformtypecode'),(967,1,'PlatformTypeCode','39','IBC Pallet','An IBC Pallet is a Rigid Intermediate Bulk Container (RIBC) that is attached to a pallet or has the pallet integrated into the RIBC. The container is used for the transport and storage of fluids and other bulk materials. The construction of the IBC container and the materials used are chosen depending on the application. There are various types available in the market place. Foldable (collapsible) IBC Container,\nPlastic composite IBC Container, Wire Cage IBC Container,\nSteel IBC Container, and Stainless steel IBC Container',NULL,'1',1,'platformtypecode'),(968,1,'PlatformTypeCode','40','Pallet 1219 X 1016 mm','ISO 3 Pallet Flat pallet with dimensions of 1219 x 1016 mm (48 x 40 In)  primarily used in the Americas region. ISO 3 Pallet',NULL,'1',1,'platformtypecode'),(969,1,'PlatformTypeCode','41','Pallet 1067 X 1067 mm','Flat pallet with dimensions of 1067 x 1067 mm (42 x 42 in) primarily used in the Americas region. ISO 4 Pallet.',NULL,'1',1,'platformtypecode'),(970,1,'PlatformTypeCode','42','Pallet 1100 X 1100 mm','Flat pallet with dimensions of 1100 x 1100 mm primarily used in the Asia Pacific region.  Also referred to as the \"T11\" pallet. ISO 5 Pallet',NULL,'1',1,'platformtypecode'),(971,1,'PlatformTypeCode','43','Pallet 1140 X 1140 mm','Flat pallet with dimensions of 1140 x 1140 mm primarily used in the European region. ISO 6 Pallet.',NULL,'1',1,'platformtypecode'),(972,1,'PlatformTypeCode','44','Skid','A group of parallel wooden runners attached to the undersides of boxes, crates, and machines to allow entry of platform trucks or fork lift tines.',NULL,'1',1,'platformtypecode'),(973,1,'PlatformTypeCode','45','Stringer Pallet','A pallet constructed with boards (stringers) on edge to which the top deck and bottom deck boards are attached. The stringers may be notched to facilitate four way entry and lifting by a fork lift or other pallet jacking device.',NULL,'1',1,'platformtypecode'),(974,1,'PlatformTypeCode','46','Vertical Drum Pallet','A rigid platform with integrated restraints to prevent vertically orientated cylindrical containers from slipping. Vertical Drum Pallets are used for assembling, storing, stacking, handling and transporting cylindrical containers, e.g. drums, barrels, or kegs, as a unit load, suitable for lifting by a forklift, pallet jack, or other jacking device.',NULL,'1',1,'platformtypecode'),(975,1,'PlatformTypeCode','47','Pallet 800 X 400 mm','One third size of the standard Euro Pallet size with dimensions of 800 x 400 mm. 1/3 European Pallet.',NULL,'1',1,'platformtypecode'),(976,1,'PlatformTypeCode','48','1/2 ISO 3 Pallet','Half size flat pallet with dimensions of 610 x 1016 mm (24 x 40 In); primarily used in the Americas region.',NULL,'1',1,'platformtypecode'),(977,1,'PlatformTypeCode','49','1/4 ISO 3 Pallet','Quarter size flat pallet with dimensions of 610 x 508 mm (24 x 20 In); primarily used in the Americas region.',NULL,'1',1,'platformtypecode'),(978,1,'PlatformTypeCode','50','Custom Platform','A portable, horizontal, rigid platform used as a base for assembling, storing, stacking, handling and transporting goods as a unit load, suitable for lifting by a forklift, pallet jack, or other jacking device.',NULL,'1',1,'platformtypecode'),(979,1,'PlatformTypeCode','9','Slip sheet','A firm sheet of plastic, cardboard or other material which may be hooked or attached to a forklift or other transportation equipment. The slip sheet is used to pull products stacked on top of it. Use packaging dimension attributes to specify the size of the slip sheet.',NULL,'1',1,'platformtypecode'),(980,1,'SizeCodeListCode','1','NRF','National Retail Federation – Standard Colour & Size Codes This handbook provides guidelines for use in retailers\' and vendors\' merchandising and communications systems.',NULL,'2',1,'sizecodelistcode'),(981,1,'SizeCodeListCode','2','Assigned by Buyer','Assigned by Buyer',NULL,'2',1,'sizecodelistcode'),(982,1,'SizeCodeListCode','3','Assigned by Seller','Assigned by Seller',NULL,'2',1,'sizecodelistcode'),(983,1,'SizeCodeListCode','4','EU Nappy/Diaper Size','EU Nappy/Diaper Size',NULL,'2',1,'sizecodelistcode'),(984,1,'SizeCodeListCode','5','North American Diaper Size','Provides the diaper size as identified by the manufacturer for the North American market',NULL,'2',1,'sizecodelistcode'),(985,1,'ColourCodeListCode','1','National Retail Federation','National Retail Federation – Standard Colour & Size Codes This handbook provides guidelines for use in retailers\' and vendors\' merchandising and communications systems.',NULL,'4',1,'colourcodelistcode'),(986,1,'ColourCodeListCode','10','NCS','NCS: Natural Colour System is a national standard for colour in Sweden, Norway, Spain and South Africa, has extensive international distribution. http://www.ncscolour.com',NULL,'4',1,'colourcodelistcode'),(987,1,'ColourCodeListCode','11','IFPS','IFPS: The International Federation for Produce Standards. IFPS is composed of national produce associations from around the globe. The long term objective of the federation is to improve the supply chain efficiency of the fresh produce industry through developing, implementing and managing harmonized international standards. http://www.ifpsglobal.com/ProductIdentification.aspx',NULL,'4',1,'colourcodelistcode'),(988,1,'ColourCodeListCode','12','sRGB','sRGB defines the chromaticities of the red, green, and blue primaries, the colours where one of the three channels is nonzero and the other two are zero. The gamut of chromaticities that can be represented in sRGB is the colour triangle defined by these primaries. As with any RGB colour space, for non-negative values of R, G, and B it is not possible to represent colours outside this triangle, which is well inside the range of colours visible to a human with normal trichromatic vision. sRGB is sometimes avoided by high-end print publishing professionals because its colour gamut is not big enough, especially in the blue-green colours, to include all the colours that can be reproduced in CMYK printing.',NULL,'4',1,'colourcodelistcode'),(989,1,'ColourCodeListCode','2','PANTONE MATCHING SYSTEM','The definitive international reference for selecting, specifying, matching and controlling ink colours. The PANTONE formula guide, a three-guide set consisting of 1,114 solid PANTONE Colours on coated, uncoated and matte stock, shows corresponding printing ink formulas for each colour, and the three-book set of solid chips provides coated, uncoated and matte perforated tear-out chips that can be used for quality control. Pantone® Inc\n',NULL,'4',1,'colourcodelistcode'),(990,1,'ColourCodeListCode','3','PANTONE Process Colour System®','Provides a comprehensive palette of more than 3,000 colours achievable in four-color (CMYK) process printing. The PANTONE solid to process guide compares a solid PANTONE Colour to the closest possible match in CMYK four-color process that can be achieved on a computer monitor, output device or printing press. Other PANTONE Colour Reference Guides for the graphic arts include metallic, pastels, tints, duotones, film and foil. The PANTONE Hexachrome® Color System. Pantone® Inc',NULL,'4',1,'colourcodelistcode'),(991,1,'ColourCodeListCode','4','The PANTONE Hexachrome® Color System','A six-colour ultra high quality printing process, reproduces a dynamic range of more brilliant continuous-tone images and simulates brighter, more vivid colours than standard four-color process printing. Pantone® Inc\n',NULL,'4',1,'colourcodelistcode'),(992,1,'ColourCodeListCode','5','PANTONE TEXTILE Colour System®','A vital tool for designers in the apparel, home furnishings and interior design industries for selecting and specifying colour used in the manufacture of textiles and fashion. The System - consisting of 1,932 colours in cotton or paper format - is ideal for assembling creative palettes and conceptual colour schemes, and for providing colour communication and control in the manufacturing process.  In January of 2001 Pantone Inc. included the NRF Colour Codes into the PANTONE TEXTILE Color System',NULL,'4',1,'colourcodelistcode'),(993,1,'ColourCodeListCode','6','Assigned by Buyer','Assigned by Buyer',NULL,'4',1,'colourcodelistcode'),(994,1,'ColourCodeListCode','7','Assigned by Seller','Assigned by Seller',NULL,'4',1,'colourcodelistcode'),(995,1,'ColourCodeListCode','8','WWS','(Waren Wirtschafts System):\nA colour code system used in Germany for the standardisation of colours within the fashion/apparel sector.',NULL,'4',1,'colourcodelistcode'),(996,1,'ColourCodeListCode','9','RAL','RAL: Farbsystem RAL colour system is an international colour standard for professional users of colours in industry, trade, architecture and design since 1927. RAL is an independent and neutral partner for industry and trade. http://www.ral.de.',NULL,'4',1,'colourcodelistcode'),(997,1,'Gs1TradeItemIdentificationKeyCode','GTIN_12','GTIN 12','The 12-digit GS1 Identification Key composed of a U.P.C. Company Prefix, Item Reference, and Check Digit used to identify trade items.',NULL,'1',1,'gs1tradeitemidentificationkeycode'),(998,1,'Gs1TradeItemIdentificationKeyCode','GTIN_13','GTIN 13','The 13-digit GS1 Identification Key composed of a GS1 Company Prefix, Item Reference, and Check Digit used to identify trade items.',NULL,'1',1,'gs1tradeitemidentificationkeycode'),(999,1,'Gs1TradeItemIdentificationKeyCode','GTIN_14','GTIN 14','The 14-digit GS1 Identification Key composed of an Indicator digit (1-9), GS1 Company Prefix, Item Reference, and Check Digit used to identify trade items.',NULL,'1',1,'gs1tradeitemidentificationkeycode'),(1000,1,'Gs1TradeItemIdentificationKeyCode','GTIN_8','GTIN 8','The 8-digit GS1 Identification Key composed of a GS1-8 Prefix, Item Reference, and Check Digit used to identify trade items.',NULL,'1',1,'gs1tradeitemidentificationkeycode'),(1001,1,'CountryCode','001','Global Market','Global Market is a way to represent information globally relevant. Examples of business Travel Retail, Duty Free Shopping. etc.',NULL,'4',1,'countrycode'),(1002,1,'CountryCode','097','European Union','European Union',NULL,'4',1,'countrycode'),(1003,1,'CountryCode','D_A','Development Assistance','Development assistance agencies such as  USAID, UNFPA, and Global Fund which provide foreign assistance to countries in the form of commodities and services to support development programs, including but not limited to global health, infrastructure, and food aid. Note, this code value can only be used for the attribute targetMarketCountryCode.\n',NULL,'4',1,'countrycode'),(1004,1,'CountryCode','NON_EU','Non EU','Country that is not in the European Union. GDSN only.',NULL,'4',1,'countrycode'),(1005,1,'CountryCode','004','Afghanistan','Afghanistan',NULL,'4',1,'countrycode'),(1006,1,'CountryCode','248','Åland Islands','Åland Islands',NULL,'4',1,'countrycode'),(1007,1,'CountryCode','008','Albania','Albania',NULL,'4',1,'countrycode'),(1008,1,'CountryCode','012','Algeria','Algeria',NULL,'4',1,'countrycode'),(1009,1,'CountryCode','016','American Samoa','American Samoa',NULL,'4',1,'countrycode'),(1010,1,'CountryCode','020','Andorra','Andorra',NULL,'4',1,'countrycode'),(1011