. A product classification system maintained by GS1 Spain and used in the Spanish Market.',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1262,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','18','GS1 Poland','GS1 Poland. A product classification system maintained by GS1 Poland.',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1263,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','19','Federal Agency on Technical Regulating and Metrology of the Russia Federation',' A Russian government agency that serves as a national standardization body of the Russian Federation.',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1264,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','2','IRI','IRI',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1265,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','20','ECR','Efficient Consumer Response (ECR) Austria',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1266,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','21','GS1 Italy','GS1 Italy',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1267,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','22','CPV','Common Procurement Vocabulary (CPV) was introduced in 1996 as a means of raising the level of transparency and efficiency in the field of public acquisition. The use of the standard names of the CPV facilitates the marking of the procurement contracts they are interested in. In addition, CPV facilitates the swift and exact translation of contract information for publication in the official EU Bulletin as well as the preparation of procurement statistics. The CPV code consists of eight characters as well as a control character.  It is managed by the Office for Official Publications of the European Communities (OPOCE).',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1268,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','23','IFDA','International Foodservice Distributors Association (IFDA)',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1269,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','24','AHFS','American Hospital Formulary Service AHFS Pharmacologic - Therapeutic Classification© (AHFS)',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1270,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','25','ATC','Anatomical Therapeutic Chemical classification (ATC)',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1271,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','26','ClaDiMed','Classification des Dispositifs Médicaux (ClaDiMed)',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1272,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','27','CMDR','Canadian Medical Device Regulations (CMDR)',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1273,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','28','CND','Classificazione Nazionale dei Dispositivi Medici (CND)',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1274,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','3','AC Nielsen','AC Nielsen',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1275,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','30','UKDM&D','UK Dictionary of Medicines & Devices( DM&D) Standard Coding Scheme',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1276,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','31','eCl@ss','Standardized Material and Service Classification and Dictionary',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1277,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','32','EDMA','Classification for in vitro diagnostics medical devices (EDMA)',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1278,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','33','EGAR','European Generic Article Register Classification (EGAR ) standard for medical devices',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1279,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','34','IMS','IMS Healthcare Generic Product Classification',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1280,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','35','GMDN','Global Medical Devices Nomenclature (GMDN)',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1281,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','36','GPI','Generic Product Identifier (GPI). A drug code list managed by Medi-Span.',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1282,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','37','HCPCS','Healthcare Common Procedure Coding System (HCPCS): Pronounced as Hick Picks.',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1283,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','38','ICPS','International Classification for Patient Safety (ICPS). For use in Field Testing in 2007-2008 (WHO).',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1284,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','39','MedDRA','Medical Dictionary for Regulatory Activities (MedDRA): An international terminology employed by the pharmaceutical industry, medical product industry and regulatory agencies throughout the entire drug development process and product post marketing activities. The current version of MedDRA (version 10.0) contains a total of 84,906 unique terms. MedDRA terminology was developed under the auspices of the International Conference on Harmonization (ICH) of Technical Requirements for Registration of Pharmaceuticals for Human Use and is a registered trademark of the International Federation of Pharmaceutical Manufacturers Associations (IFPMA).',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1285,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','4','GS1 Canada ECCnet','A product classification system ECCnet Classification Codes maintained by GS1 Canada and used by the GS1 Canada ECCnet Registry.',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1286,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','40','Medical Columbus','German Medical classification system.',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1287,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','41','NAPCS','North American Classification System (NAPCS)',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1288,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','42','NHS-eClass','National Health Service (NHS) eClass:  NHS-eClass is a bespoke classification system for products and services, owned by the English National Health Service (NHS). The purpose of NHS-eClass is to facilitate the accurate analysis of expenditure.',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1289,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','43','US FDA PCCD','The Product Classification Database contains medical device names and associated information developed by the Center for Devices and Radiological Health (CDRH) in support of its mission. This database contains device names and their associated product codes. The name and product code identify the generic category of a device for FDA. The Product Code assigned to a device is based upon the medical device product classification designated under 21 CFR Parts 862-892.',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1290,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','44','SHPA','The Society of Hospital Pharmacists of Australia (SHPA)',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1291,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','45','SNOMED CT','Systematized Nomenclature of Medicine-Clinical Terms ( SNOMED CT® )',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1292,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','46','UMDNS','Universal Medical Device Nomenclature System (UMDNS)',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1293,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','47','DTB','DTB (fashion) Dialog Textil – Bekleiding (DTB) a German group of companies who joined forces for the TC sector. The product classification can be found on their website http://www.dialog-dtb.de if you are a member.',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1294,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','48','FEDAS PCK','SGI-DHO (Sporting Goods Industry Data Harmonization Organization) is representing the interests of the different stakeholders of the sporting goods industry (retailers + brands). Its main task is the development and harmonisation of codes, which can be used by the sporting goods industry to exchange and analyse data. The focus is set on codes that have not already been standardised by international trade organisations. \nIn addition to the FEDAS (the European Federation of Sporting Goods Retail Associations) product classification key that has been developed a few years ago, and which is used by may stakeholders of the sporting goods industry, SGI-DHO is working on various other codes. \nUnder www.sgidho.com you can find further information. ',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1295,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','49','EAS','EAS (footwear) European Article System: A harmonised system to classify and process the characteristics of shoes across Europe.',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1296,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','5','UNSPSC','United Nations Standard Products and Services Code',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1297,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','50','Australian TGA Type','The Australian Therapeutic Goods Administration (TGA) classifies products it authorizes for sale in Australia. These items are considered either: Registered, Listed, Included or Classified as Other on the Australia Register of Therapeutic Goods (ARTG). ',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1298,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','51','Australian Medicines and Poisons Schedule Code','SUSMP: An  Australian classification and labelling of drugs and poisons named the Standard for the Uniform Scheduling of Medicines and Poisons (SUSMP). This was created and is maintained by the National Drugs and Poisons Scheduling Committee (NDPSC) which operates under control of the Therapeutic Goods Administration (TGA). This standard contains a list of \'Schedules\', which are a way of grouping products together that may have similar regulatory controls over their availability. Criteria for scheduling may include such considerations as the purpose of use, potential for abuse, safety of use and the level of need for it.',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1299,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','52','Australian Pharmaceutical Benefits Scheme','In Australia, medicine may be subsidized by its Government via the Pharmaceutical Benefits Scheme (PBS). The PBS is a program available to all Australian residents covered under the public healthcare system (known as Medicare). The Pharmaceutical Benefits Schedule lists all drugs available under the scheme and the conditions under which it may be used.\nThe PBS is a way of the Australian government subsidising the cost of particular medicines to make them more affordable for the community. E.g. A consumer is entitled to purchase 100 tablets of aspirin under the scheme, the retail cost is $13.00, the government subsidizes $9.50, so the consumer will pay the difference of $3.50 for the medication.\nThe Repatriation Pharmaceutical Benefits Scheme is effectively the same scheme, however, offered to eligible war veterans, war widows and their dependents.',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1300,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','53','Australian TGA Risk Classification','The Therapeutic Goods Administration (TGA) have their own classification system for medical devices within Healthcare. The purpose of this classification is to ascertain the potential risk of a device through analysing the intended purpose of the product and using a set of classification rules. This classification allows the regulator to determine how much intervention is required before the device becomes available on the market.',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1301,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','54','MIV-C','Milch Industrie Verband Cheese Class association of the German Dairy.',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1302,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','55','MIV-D','Milch Industrie Verband Milk Class (association of the German Dairy',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1303,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','56','BTE','Bundesverband des Deutschen Textileinzelhandels a German Association of Textile Retailers. The product classification can be found on their website http://www.bte.de',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1304,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','57','REV','REV – The Office of the Revenue Commissioners: The Irish Government agency responsible for customs, excise, taxation and related matters. The division “Customs” of this office assigns classification codes to Alcohol and Tobacco for excise duties.',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1305,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','58','FDA Premarket Submission Number','FDA Premarket Submission Number is a number associated with the regulatory decision regarding the applicant’s legal right to market a medical device for the following submission types: Premarket Notification (510(k))Premarket Approval (PMA)\nProduct Development (PDP)\nHumanitarian Device Exemption (HDE)\nBiologics License Application (BLA)\nNew Drug Application (NDA).',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1306,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','59','ETIM','ETIM - (Europees Technisch Informatie Model or European Technical Information Model in English) is an international organisation which develops, manages and publishes one European classification for technical products. More information: http://www.etim-international.com/.',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1307,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','6','ECCMA','ECCMA - Electronic Commerce Code Management Association',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1308,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','60','G-DRG','G-DRG (German - Diagnosis Related Groups). [DRG-Entgeltkatalog] List of fees for treatment in German hospitals. Includes flat fees for entire courses of treatment (DRG) as well as additional fees for supplementary treatment components. The national associations of health insurance, the Association of Private Health Insurance and the German Hospital Federation, founded the Institute for the Hospital Remuneration System (InEK GmbH). The Institute InEK GmbH operates on behalf of the shareholders of the GmbH, the German Hospital Association, the Association of Statutory Health Insurance Funds and the Association of private health insurance. http://www.g-drg.de/cms/',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1309,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','61','ICD-GM','ICD-GM (International Classification of Diseases – German Modification). [Diagnosen für Gesundheitsverwaltung] German modification of the International Classification of Diseases; official classification of diseases for ambulatory and stationary care in Germany. ICD was created by the World Health Organisation, and DIMDI (Deutsches Institut für Medizinische Dokumentation und Information) maintains the German modification to ICD http://www.dimdi.de/',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1310,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','62','OPS-G','OPS-G [Operationen- und Prozedurenschlüssel] List of codes for surgical and other medical procedures, derived from the ICPM (International Classification of Procedures in Medicine), mandatory for procedure coding in hospitals and for ambulatory surgery in Germany. ICPM is maintained by the World Health Organisation, and DIMDI (Deutsches Institut für Medizinische Dokumentation und Information) maintains the German modification to it. http://www.dimdi.de/',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1311,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','63','NCM','Mercosur/Mercosul Nomenclature (NCM):   NCM is Nomenclatura Comum do MERCOSUL (MERCOSUR Common Nomenclature) Brazil, Argentina, Paraguay and Uruguay adopted the Mercosul Common Nomenclature (NCM), based on the Harmonized System Code. The eight numbers that is part of the NCM, uses the Harmonized System that forms the six first numbers, while the seventh and eighth numbers are used for specific within Mercosul. Harmonized System: The Harmonised Commodity Description and Coding System (HS) of tariff nomenclature is an internationally standardized system of names and numbers for classifying traded products developed and maintained by the World Customs Organization (WCO) (formerly the Customs Co-operation Council), an independent intergovernmental organization with over 170 member countries based in Brussels, Belgium. Example: 0104.10.11',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1312,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','64','CORE DIY','CORE DIY (Consumer Retail Classification for the Do-it-Yourself Industry) is a system for the classification of trade items with expanded product properties and specifications which provide the granularity needed for online consumer retail. CORE DIY has been developed by the do-it-yourself industry and is managed by GS1 Netherlands on behalf of the DIY user community.',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1313,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','65','FDA Preferred Term Code, ','FDA Preferred Term Code, Unique four-character value assigned by the FDA to indicate a GMDN Preferred Term without exposing the GMDN PT Code.',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1314,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','66','Medsafe Risk Classification    ','Medsafe Risk Classification               The New Zealand Medical    Devices Safety Authority',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1315,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','67','Medsafe Regulatory Classification ',' Medsafe Regulatory Classification    The New Zealand Medicines Safety Authority        ',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1316,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','68','LPRR','LPPR (List of Products and Healthcare Services Qualifying for Reimbursement) is defined by French social security and provided for in Article L-165-1 of the Code of Social Security as a nomenclature that lists medical devices for the diagnosis, treatment diseases (e.g. diabetes) or injury (bandages), hardware support everyday life, orthotics and external prostheses, implantable devices or vehicles for the physically disabled. For each product the LPPR is applied with the refundable amount, the repayment rate and possibly its end date of repayment.\n',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1317,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','69','INN','International Non-proprietary Names (INN) facilitate the identification of pharmaceutical substances or active pharmaceutical ingredients. Each INN is a unique name that is globally recognized and is public property. A non-proprietary name is also known as a generic name.',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1318,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','7','EAN Norges Multibransje Varegruppestandard','EAN Norges Multibransje Varegruppestandard - The ENVA code is used for classification and categorising of goods and it is used as an alternative to the GPC codes in the Norwegian marketplace',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1319,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','70','VBN','Vereiniging van Bloemenveilingen in Nederland, Dutch Flower Auction Association. http://www.vbn.nl/en-US/Pages/default.aspx.',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1320,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','71','Groupement d’Etude des Marchés en Restauration Collective et de Nutrition ','Groupement d’Etude des Marchés en Restauration Collective et de Nutrition - French government agency that is responsible for nutritional quality of meals served in social catering.',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1321,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','72','European Community School Milk','Program defined by the European Community to ensure milk products consumption at school.',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1322,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','73','OKPD2 Russian Classification of Product by Economic Activities.','OKPD2 Russian Classification of Product by Economic Activities.',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1323,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','74','French Ministry of Health','The French Ministry of Health is the agency in charge of the code list defining the healthcare product content (and possible associated risks) for the French market.',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1324,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','75','GS1 Sweden Alcoholic Beverages ','Product Classification System for Alcohol Beverages managed by GS1 Sweden.',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1325,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','76','EU Med Device Classification','The European medical device classification system is managed by the European Commission, the European Parliament and the Council of Ministers.',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1326,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','77','MiGeL Position number','The MiGeL item number regulates the reimbursement of medical products in the outpatient sector and is information that is required by all service providers in Switzerland in order to be able to bill service carriers.  MiGel-Number applies to similar items across suppliers that have the  identical number.',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1327,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','8','Supplier Assigned','A manufacturer\'s own codification system',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1328,1,'AdditionalTradeItemClassificationCodeListCode','9','AMECE','AMECE - Code system used in the GS1 Mexico market',NULL,'9',1,'additionaltradeitemclassificationcodelistcode'),(1329,1,'NonfoodIngredientOfConcernCode','BFR_HFR','Halogenated Organic Flame Retardants','Halogenated organic flame retardants are intended to inhibit ignition and the spread of flames. Halogenated chemicals are chemicals that contain bromine, chlorine, fluorine or iodine bonded to a carbon atom. ',NULL,'1',1,'nonfoodingredientofconcerncode'),(1330,1,'NonfoodIngredientOfConcernCode','BPA','Bisphenol','Bisphenol is an organic compound with the chemical formula (CH3)2C(C6H4OH)2. It is a colourless solid that is soluble in organic solvents, but poorly soluble in water. BPA is controversial because it exerts weak, but detectable, hormone-like properties, raising concerns about its presence in consumer products and foods contained in such products',NULL,'1',1,'nonfoodingredientofconcerncode'),(1331,1,'NonfoodIngredientOfConcernCode','DEHP','DEHP','Di-(2-ethylhexyl) phthalate (DEHP) is a member of the phthalate family used as a softening agent for many PVC applications.  DEHP is sometimes called dioctyl phthalate (DOP) or Bis(2-ethylhexyl)phthalate (BEHP).  In the EU package markings require a mark to show \"PHT\".',NULL,'1',1,'nonfoodingredientofconcerncode'),(1332,1,'NonfoodIngredientOfConcernCode','HG','Mercury','Mercury is a naturally occurring element that is found in air, water and soil. It exists in several forms: elemental or metallic mercury, inorganic mercury compounds, and organic mercury compounds.',NULL,'1',1,'nonfoodingredientofconcerncode'),(1333,1,'NonfoodIngredientOfConcernCode','PAPER_WOOD','Paper or Wood','If any portion of this item, including reusable packaging, is made from wood or paper, then answer “Yes”. Reusable packaging is intended to stay in use with the product. Ex: Wooden box in which a lawn game, such as a croquet set, is stored after use. ',NULL,'1',1,'nonfoodingredientofconcerncode'),(1334,1,'NonfoodIngredientOfConcernCode','PS','Polystyrene (CAS 9003-53-6)','Polystyrene (CAS 9003-53-6) is a plastic polymer from the monomer styrene. It comes in many forms: sheet, expanded or extruded foam, or as oriented polystyrene. What is commonly known as Styrofoam™ refers only to the extruded form of polystyrene.',NULL,'1',1,'nonfoodingredientofconcerncode'),(1335,1,'NonfoodIngredientOfConcernCode','PVC','Polyvinyl chloride (PVC) ','Polyvinyl chloride (PVC) is a plastic polymer used in a wide array of products. It is the third most widely produced plastic.',NULL,'1',1,'nonfoodingredientofconcerncode'),(1336,1,'TradeItemUnitDescriptorCode','BASE_UNIT_OR_EACH','Base Unit or Each','The lowest level of the item hierarchy intended or labeled for individual resale.',NULL,'1',1,'tradeitemunitdescriptorcode'),(1337,1,'TradeItemUnitDescriptorCode','CASE','Case','A standard trade item shipping unit that contains a single or multiple GTINs. Includes an ½ or ¼ pallet and an ½ or ¼ box pallet.',NULL,'1',1,'tradeitemunitdescriptorcode'),(1338,1,'TradeItemUnitDescriptorCode','DISPLAY_SHIPPER','Display Shipper','A display, a shipper. May have a “PL” parent. May have (CA or EA) children in multiple instances. It may be Orderable and can be a Consumer Unit.',NULL,'1',1,'tradeitemunitdescriptorcode'),(1339,1,'TradeItemUnitDescriptorCode','MIXED_MODULE','Mixed Module','A unit load that is a “display ready pallet” that may contain a single GTIN or several unique GTINs that is intended to go directly to the selling floor',NULL,'1',1,'tradeitemunitdescriptorcode'),(1340,1,'TradeItemUnitDescriptorCode','PACK_OR_INNER_PACK','Pack or Inner Pack','A logistical unit between case and each. This may be a consumable innerpack (i.e. Carton of Cigarettes) or it may be simply a logistical pack (i.e. Dozes of toothbrushes).',NULL,'1',1,'tradeitemunitdescriptorcode'),(1341,1,'TradeItemUnitDescriptorCode','PALLET','Pallet','A unit load that contains a single or multiple GTINs Includes box pallet',NULL,'1',1,'tradeitemunitdescriptorcode'),(1342,1,'TradeItemUnitDescriptorCode','TRANSPORT_LOAD','Transport Load','Trade item above the pallet level used for transporting trade items. For example truck load, container, rail car, ship, etc.',NULL,'1',1,'tradeitemunitdescriptorcode'),(1343,1,'ImportClassificationTypeCode','CTCURBK',NULL,'Customs Tariff Of The Customs Union Between Russia Belarus And Kazakhstan',NULL,'2',1,'importclassificationtypecode'),(1344,1,'ImportClassificationTypeCode','CUSTOMS_TARIFF_NUMBER',NULL,'NOT AVAILABLE',NULL,'2',1,'importclassificationtypecode'),(1345,1,'ImportClassificationTypeCode','EU_EXCISE_PRODUCT_CODE',NULL,'EU classification of the products that are subjected to excise duties : http://goo.gl/Q671jF',NULL,'2',1,'importclassificationtypecode'),(1346,1,'ImportClassificationTypeCode','FEACNRF',NULL,'Foreign Economic Activity Commodity Nomenclature of Russian Federation',NULL,'2',1,'importclassificationtypecode'),(1347,1,'ImportClassificationTypeCode','HARMONIZED_COMMODITY_DESCRIPTION_AND_CODING_SYSTEM',NULL,'An internationally standardized system of names and numbers for classifying traded products developed and maintained by the World Customs Organization (WCO)',NULL,'2',1,'importclassificationtypecode'),(1348,1,'ImportClassificationTypeCode','HARMONIZED_TARIFF_SCHEDULE_OF_THE_US',NULL,'Tariff classifications for goods imported into the United States',NULL,'2',1,'importclassificationtypecode'),(1349,1,'ImportClassificationTypeCode','INTRASTAT',NULL,'A system for collecting information and producing statistics on the trade in goods between countries of the European Union (EU).',NULL,'2',1,'importclassificationtypecode'),(1350,1,'ImportClassificationTypeCode','INTRASTAT_COMBINED_NOMENCLATURE',NULL,'Collection of commodity codes used with the European Union.',NULL,'2',1,'importclassificationtypecode'),(1351,1,'ImportClassificationTypeCode','MERCOSUR',NULL,'A regional trade agreement created in 1991, and it is integrated by Brazil, Argentina, Uruguay, Paraguay and Venezuela.',NULL,'2',1,'importclassificationtypecode'),(1352,1,'ImportClassificationTypeCode','NETHERLANDS',NULL,'Netherlands',NULL,'2',1,'importclassificationtypecode'),(1353,1,'ImportClassificationTypeCode','NOMENCLATURE_GENERALE_DES_PRODUITS',NULL,'This import classification type is a French supplement to the European combined nomenclature.',NULL,'2',1,'importclassificationtypecode'),(1354,1,'ImportClassificationTypeCode','TARIF_INTEGRE_DE_LA_COMMUNAUTE',NULL,'Integrated Tariff of the European Community',NULL,'2',1,'importclassificationtypecode'),(1355,1,'ImportClassificationTypeCode','TN_VED',NULL,'A commodity nomenclature of foreign-economic activity in Commonwealth of Independent States.',NULL,'2',1,'importclassificationtypecode'),(1356,1,'RegulationTypeCode','AEROSOL_REVERSE_EPSILON','Aerosol Reverse Epsilon','Products complying with all the requirements of the Aerosol Directive are marked with the \"reverse epsilon\" symbol',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1357,1,'RegulationTypeCode','AGRICULTURE_PROTECTION_REGULATION','Agriculture Protection Regulation','Products complying with EU Council Directive 91/414/EEC. This directive concerning the placing of plant protection products on the market lays down rules and procedures for approval of the active substances at EU-level and for the authorisation at Member State level of plant protection products (PPPs) containing these substances. This Directive states that substances cannot be used in plant protection products unless they are included in a positive EU list. Once a substance is included in the positive list Member States may authorise the use of products containing them.',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1358,1,'RegulationTypeCode','ANIMAL_ID_HEALTH_MARK','Animal ID Health Mark','Food business operators, in accordance with Regulation (EC) No 853/2004, should ensure that all products of animal origin that they place on the market, bear either a health mark or an identification mark.',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1359,1,'RegulationTypeCode','BATTERY_DIRECTIVE','Battery Directive','Directive describing the legal requirements on batteries intended to made available on the market provided that such products are labelled, marked or accompanied with commercial documents. Essentially safety and environmental aspects are defined (e.g. obligation of the seller to take batteries back, proscription to throw batteries into the household garbage) for different type of batteries (e.g. batteries used by the end consumer, batteries used in cars). In Germany the law on batteries (BattG) details these rules.',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1360,1,'RegulationTypeCode','BIOCIDE_REGULATION','Biocide Regulation','The purpose of this Regulation (EU Reg 528/2012) is to harmonise the rules on making available on the market and using biocidal products, whilst ensuring a high level of protection of both human and animal health and the environment. These rules compasses the establishment a list of active substances which may be used in biocidal products and the authorisation of biocidal products.',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1361,1,'RegulationTypeCode','CE','CE','The CE marking as it has been legally called since 1993 (per directive 93/68/EEC)(DECISION No 768/2008/EC) (abbreviation of French: Conformité Européenne, meaning \"European Conformity\"[1], formerly EC mark[2]) is a mandatory conformity mark for products placed on the market in the European Economic Area (EEA).',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1362,1,'RegulationTypeCode','COMPLIANT_WITH_FAIR_LABOR_STANDARDS_ACT','Compliant with Fairl Labor Standards Act','The FLSA established a national minimum wage guaranteed \'time-and-a-half\' for overtime in certain jobs, and prohibited most employment of minors in \"oppressive child labor,\" a term that is defined in the statute. It applies to employees engaged in interstate commerce or employed by an enterprise engaged in commerce or in the production of goods for commerce, unless the employer can claim an exemption from coverage.',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1363,1,'RegulationTypeCode','COMPLIANT_WITH_FLAMMABILITY_ACT','Compliant with Flammability Act','NOT AVAILABLE',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1364,1,'RegulationTypeCode','COMPLIANT_WITH_FUR_PRODUCT_LABELING_ACT','Compliant with Fur Product Labelling Act','Requires the country of origin of imported furs to be disclosed on all labels and in all advertising',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1365,1,'RegulationTypeCode','COMPLIANT_WITH_STATE_ENVIRONMENT_REQUIREMENTS','Compliant with State Environment Requirements','NOT AVAILABLE',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1366,1,'RegulationTypeCode','COMPLIANT_WITH_TEXTILE_FIBER_PRODUCT_IDENTIFICATION','Compliant with Textile Fiber Product Identification','A US regulation regarding the advertising and labelling of textile fibre products.',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1367,1,'RegulationTypeCode','COMPLIANT_WITH_WOOL_PRODUCTS_LABELING_ACT','Compliant with Wool Products Labelling Act','A US regulation that requires anyone who manufacturers or sells products containing wool to accurately label each item with the fibre content and origin',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1368,1,'RegulationTypeCode','CONSUMER_PRODUCT_SAFETY','Consumer Product Safety','A regulation concerning consumer product safety when a government regulates certain products for safety like child car seats, baby cribs etc., For example in the US Consumer Product Safety Commission (CPSC): official Federal Agency including recalls, reports, alerts about products regulated. ',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1369,1,'RegulationTypeCode','CONTAINS_COMPOSITE_WOOD','Contains Composite Wood','Describes that the trade item or packaging contains composite wood that falls under regulatory menas due to chemicals used in process to create the wood, such as Formaldehyde  has both cancer and noncancer-causing effects on human health. For example:  California Air Resources Board is a department of the California Environmental Protection Agency. CARB’s mission, US EPA. https://www.epa.gov/formaldehyde .',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1370,1,'RegulationTypeCode','COSMETIC_INFORMATION_REGULATION','Cosmetic Information Regulation','Regulation (EU Reg 1223/2009) establishing rules to be complied with any cosmetic product made available on the market, a high level of protection of human health and a high degree of protection of the environment. These rules include the necessity to indicate allergens and the displaying of the ingredients used in the product.',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1371,1,'RegulationTypeCode','DETERGENTS_SAFETY_REGULATION','Detergents Safety Regulation','Regulation  establishing rules designed to achieve the free movement of detergents and surfactants for detergents in the market while, at the same time, ensuring a high degree of protection of the environment and human health. For example (EU Reg 648/2004) ',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1372,1,'RegulationTypeCode','E_MARK','E Mark','The Estimated Sign (℮) (also referred to as \"e-mark\") is a mark that sometimes can be found on pre-packed goods in Europe. The e-mark indicates that the packaging is filled according to the European Directive 76/211/EEC.',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1373,1,'RegulationTypeCode','EFFICIENCY_OF_LAMPS_LUMINARIES','Efficiency of Lamps Luminaries','A directive defining the energy labeling of electrical lamps and luminaires (e.g. EU Reg 874/2012). This directive deals with environmental aspects as the electricity used by electrical lamps accounts for a significant share of total electricity demand.',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1374,1,'RegulationTypeCode','EMC_DIRECTIVE','EMC Directive','The main objective of the Directive 2004/108/EC of the European Council, of 15 December 2004, is to regulate the compatibility of equipment regarding EMC (Electromagnetic Compatibility).',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1375,1,'RegulationTypeCode','ENCLOSED_ATTACHED_INFORMATION','Enclosed Attached Information','Indicates the product contains enclosed or attached information available for regulatory compliance where applicable.',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1376,1,'RegulationTypeCode','ENERGY_GUIDE_LABEL_REQUIRED','Energy Guide Label Required','A code that indicates that a trade item is in compliance with energy efficiency guide and is labelled as such.',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1377,1,'RegulationTypeCode','EU_REGULATION_FOR_FOODSTUFF','EU Regulation for Foodstuff','Regulation (EC) No 178/2002 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 28 January 2002 laying down the general principles and requirements of food law, establishing the European Food Safety Authority and laying down procedures in matters of food safety. \nFor the purposes of this Regulation, \"food\" (or \"foodstuff\") means any substance or product, whether processed, partially processed or unprocessed, intended to be, or reasonably expected to be ingested by humans. \"Food\" includes: drink, chewing gum and any substance, including water, intentionally incorporated into the food during its manufacture, preparation or treatment. It includes water after the point of compliance.',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1378,1,'RegulationTypeCode','FEED_SAFETY_REGULATION','Feed Safety Regulation','Regulation (EU Reg 767/2009) to harmonise the conditions for the placing on the market and the use of feed, in order to ensure a high level of feed safety and thus a high level of protection of public health, as well as to provide adequate information for users and consumers. ',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1379,1,'RegulationTypeCode','FOOD_FOR_SPECIAL_PURPOSES','Food For Special Purposes','Regulation providing the basis for the assurance of a high level of consumer protection in relation to specialized food like food for infants and young children, food for special medical purposes, and total diet replacement for weight control (e.g. EU Reg 609/2013).',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1380,1,'RegulationTypeCode','FOOD_INFORMATION_REGULATION','Food Information Regulation','Regulation providing the basis for the assurance of a high level of consumer protection in relation to food information, taking into account the differences in the perception of consumers and their information needs whilst ensuring the smooth functioning of the market. General principles, requirements and responsibilities governing food information, and in particular food labelling rules are established (e.g. EU regulation 1169 / 2011). These rules include the necessity to indicate allergens, the responsible food business operator, the name of the food, the displaying of the ingredients used additives.',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1381,1,'RegulationTypeCode','FOOD_LABELLING_UNDER_2_YEARS_OF_AGE','Food Labelling Under 2 Years of Age','Foods, other than infant formula, represented or purported to be specifically for infants and children less than 2 years of age shall bear nutrition labelling.',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1382,1,'RegulationTypeCode','FOOD_LABELLING_UNDER_4_YEARS_OF_AGE','Food Labelling Under 4 Years of Age','Foods, other than infant formula, represented or purported to be specifically for infants and children less than 4 years of age shall bear nutrition labelling.',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1383,1,'RegulationTypeCode','FOOD_SUPPLEMENT_DIRECTIVE','Food Supplement Directive','Food supplements (EU directive 2002/46/EC) marketed as foodstuffs and presented as such. These products shall be delivered to the ultimate consumer only in a pre-packaged form. Consumer health and safety aspects are in focus as well as to provide adequate information on how to use the product properly. ',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1384,1,'RegulationTypeCode','FREE_PHARMACEUTICAL_PRODUCTS_DIRECTIVE','Free Pharmaceutical Products Directive','Directive describing the legal requirements on pharmaceutical products which are commercially available and intended to made available on the market provided that such products are labelled, marked or accompanied with commercial documents. General Consumer safety aspects are in focus like the dosage form linked with an application instruction (e.g. Do not use with alcohol). In Germany the law on medical products (AMG) details these rules.',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1385,1,'RegulationTypeCode','FRENCH_SPARE_PARTS_REGULATION','French Spare Parts Regulation','Decree No. 2014-1482 of 9 December 2014 on the information and supply obligations concerning spare parts indispensable for the use of a good.',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1386,1,'RegulationTypeCode','HERBICIDE_REGULATION','Herbicide Regulation','The item is a substance used to control unwanted plants that are subject to regulation.',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1387,1,'RegulationTypeCode','INFANT_FORMULA_LABELLING','Infant formula Labelling','Infant formula except foods, shall be labelled in compliance with regulations.',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1388,1,'RegulationTypeCode','INTENDED_TO_COME_INTO_CONTACT_WITH_FOOD','Intended to Come Into Contact With Food','Requires that food contact materials a re safe; Must not transfer their components into food in quantities that could endanger human health, change food composition in an unacceptable way or deteriorate its taste and odour. Are manufactured according to good manufacturing practice.',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1389,1,'RegulationTypeCode','LVD_DIRECTIVE','LVD Directive','The Low Voltage Directive (LVD) 2006/95/EC provides common broad objectives for safety regulations, so that electrical equipment approved by any EU member country will be acceptable for use in all other EU countries. The Low Voltage Directive does not supply any specific technical standards that must be met, instead relying on IEC technical standards to guide designers to produce safe products. Products that conform to the general principles of the Low Voltage Directive and the relevant particular safety standards are marked with the CE marking to indicate compliance and acceptance throughout the EU. Conformance is asserted by the manufacturer based on its conformity assessment.',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1390,1,'RegulationTypeCode','MEDICAL_DEVICE_SAFETY','Medical Device Safety','A directive establishing common rules on the safety, health protection and performance characteristics of medical devices in order to provide the safety and health protection of patients, users and, where appropriate, other persons, with regard to the use of medical devices (e.g. DIRECTIVE 93/42/EEC of the European Council).\n',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1391,1,'RegulationTypeCode','MINIMUM_DURABILITY','Minimum Durability','Indicates the product has a regulatory requirement to show to the consumer the best to use before period so they obtain the full functionality of the product.',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1392,1,'RegulationTypeCode','NANO_MATERIALS_PRESENCE','Nano Materials Presence','Indicates the presence of nano materials by the levels acceptable by the appropriate regulation.',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1393,1,'RegulationTypeCode','PACKAGING_SAFETY_DIRECTIVE','Packaging Safety Directive','The product represented in its packaging and/or marketing as appropriate for use by persons as defined by regulatory agency?  Includes packaging, display, photography, licensed characters, promotion or advertising (in-store or ad) as appropriate for use by persons. An example is the Consumer Product Safety Commission regulation: https://www.cpsc.gov/Regulations-Laws--Standards/Statutes/Poison-Prevention-Packaging-Act/Child-Resistant-and-Senior-Friendly-Packages-packaging-guide/.',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1394,1,'RegulationTypeCode','PERIOD_SAFE_TO_USE_AFTER_OPENING','Period Safe To Use After Opening','Indicates the product has a regulatory requirement to show to the consumer that product is denoted to have a period of time after opening before it becomes harmful to the consumer.',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1395,1,'RegulationTypeCode','PESTICIDE_REGULATION','Pesticide Regulation','The item is a substance used to control unwanted pests that are subject to regulation.',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1396,1,'RegulationTypeCode','PHARMACEUTICAL_PRODUCT_DIRECTIVE','Pharmaceutical Product Directive','In contrast to the free pharmaceutical directive this directive describing the legal requirements on pharmaceutical products available only in pharmacies. These products have stronger regulations and restrictions to consumer safety aspects. For example the dosage recommendation needs to be explained in detail by the sales staff as well as possible interaction with other pharmaceutical products.',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1397,1,'RegulationTypeCode','PRODUCT_OF_DAILY_USE_DIRECTIVE','Product of Daily Use Directive','Directive describing the legal requirements on the products of daily use focusing on consumer safety (e.g. do not use with …, not used by children). An example is the German directive BedGgstV.',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1398,1,'RegulationTypeCode','PROP_65','Prop 65','Containing specific toxicants for a product which contains carcinogens and/or reproductive toxicants established in California’s Proposition 65 (Prop 65), The Safe Drinking Water and Toxic Enforcement Act, enacted in 1986.  This Act requires the state to publish a list of chemicals known to cause cancer or reproductive harm. Prop 65 applies to suppliers who sell products in the state if their products exceed safe harbour levels established in Prop 65. Safe harbour levels establish thresholds for no significant risk levels (NSRLs) for carcinogens and maximum allowable dose levels (MADLs) for chemicals that cause reproductive toxicity. ',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1399,1,'RegulationTypeCode','REGULATED_BY_AGENCY','Regulated by Agency','The trade item is regulated by the agency stated in the regulatoryAgency attribute.',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1400,1,'RegulationTypeCode','RETURNING_OF_ELECTRONICAL_PRODUCT_DIRECTIVE','Returning of Electronic Product Directive',' Directive of the returning of electronic products ensuring a high degree of protection of the environment. This directive defines returning quotes of returning electronical products needs to be fulfilled by the industry and by retailers (e.g. ElektroG in Germany).',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1401,1,'RegulationTypeCode','ROHS_DIRECTIVE','ROHS Directive','Is not a quality mark but a European directive 2002/95/EC (stands for Restriction of Hazardous Substances). This directive restricts (with exceptions) the use of six hazardous materials like lead, cadmium and mercury in the manufacture of various types of electronic and electrical equipment.',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1402,1,'RegulationTypeCode','SECURITY_OF_ELECTRONIC_PRODUCTS_DIRECTIVE','Security of Electronic Products Directive','Directive on the safety of electronic products covering consumer health as well as environmental aspects (e.g. German law on product safety ProdSG).',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1403,1,'RegulationTypeCode','TEXTILE_LABELLING_REGULATION','Textile Labelling Regulation','Regulation (EU Reg 1007/2011). This Regulation lays down rules concerning the use of textile fibre names and related labelling and marking of fibre composition of textile products, rules concerning the labelling or marking of textile products containing non-textile parts of animal origin and rules concerning the determination of the fibre composition of textile products by quantitative analysis of binary and ternary textile fibre mixtures, in order to provide accurate information to consumers.',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1404,1,'RegulationTypeCode','TOY_SAFETY_DIRECTIVE','Toy Safety Directive','Directive, which applies to products designed or intended, whether or not exclusively, for use in play by children under 14 years of age. Health and safety aspects of the child are in focus Amongst others security aspects of toys are defined (e.g. Warning: small components may be swallowed) as well as substances, which are not allowed to use in toys (e.g. softening agents).',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1405,1,'RegulationTypeCode','TRACEABILITY_REGULATION','Traceability Regulation','Indicates that a trade item  is subject to government rules and regulations regarding traceability. ',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1406,1,'RegulationTypeCode','TRADE_ITEM_TESTED_DIRECTIVE','Trade Item Tested Directive','The product has conformed to testing requirements to meet regulation needs. An example is the Consumer Product Safety Commission https://www.cpsc.gov/Regulations-Laws--Standards/Statutes/The-Consumer-Product-Safety-Improvement-Act/.',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1407,1,'RegulationTypeCode','TREATED_WITH_HERBICIDE_REGULATION','Treated with Herbicide Regulation','Trade item has been treated with herbicide(s) that are subject to regulation.',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1408,1,'RegulationTypeCode','TREATED_WITH_PESTICIDE_REGULATION','Treated with Pesticide Regulation.','Trade item has been treated with pesticide(s) that are subject to regulation.',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1409,1,'RegulationTypeCode','UNDERWATER_LIGHTING','Underwater Lighting','The European standard EN 60598-2-18 is recognized by most countries as the safety standard for underwater lighting.',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1410,1,'RegulationTypeCode','UVA','UVA','EU 647 Cosmetic industry worked closely with the European Commission, and COLIPA, currently called COSMETICS EUROPE proposed a UVA labelling symbol. This indicates that the level of UVA protection provided by a product is at least 1/3 ratio of its SPF.  Manufacturers will show that their products meet the SPF/UVAPF ratio by displaying the letters “UVA” inside a circle whose diameter should not exceed the height of the SPF number. ',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1411,1,'RegulationTypeCode','VOLATILE_ORGANIC_COMPOUND_COMPLIANT','Volatile Organic Compound Compliant','Organic chemicals that have a high vapor pressure at ordinary, room-temperature conditions. Their high vapor pressure results from a low boiling point, which causes large numbers of molecules to evaporate or sublimate from the liquid or solid form of the compound and enter the surrounding air',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1412,1,'RegulationTypeCode','BPA_REGULATION','BPA Regulation ','Indicates the product has a regulatory requirement to show to the consumer that it may or may not contain Bisphenol A (BPA). ',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1413,1,'RegulationTypeCode','MARKET_AUTHORISATION','Market Authorisation','The trade item has been authorised to be sold by a regulatory agency to be distributed in a market.',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1414,1,'RegulationTypeCode','PRODUCT_LABELING_REGULATION','Product Labelling Regulation','A code indicating the trade item is compliant with the food labelling regulation.',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1415,1,'RegulationTypeCode','VEHICLE_LICENSE_PLATE_REGISTRATION','Vehicle License Plate Registration ','Provides proof of the registered motorized vehicle plate number.',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1416,1,'RegulationTypeCode','VEHICLE_LIGHTING_COMPLIANT','Vehicle Lighting Compliant','Vehicle lighting meets regulatory compliance in road and off road safety. Example in the US is SAE-DOT',NULL,'6',1,'regulationtypecode'),(1417,1,'LanguageCode','aa','Afar',NULL,NULL,'1',1,'languagecode'),(1418,1,'LanguageCode','ab','Abkhazian',NULL,NULL,'1',1,'languagecode'),(1419,1,'LanguageCode','ae','Avestan',NULL,NULL,'1',1,'languagecode'),(1420,1,'LanguageCode','af','Afrikaans',NULL,NULL,'1',1,'languagecode'),(1421,1,'LanguageCode','ak','Akan',NULL,NULL,'1',1,'languagecode'),(1422,1,'LanguageCode','am','Amharic',NULL,NULL,'1',1,'languagecode'),(1423,1,'LanguageCode','an','Aragonese',NULL,NULL,'1',1,'languagecode'),(1424,1,'LanguageCode','ar','Arabic',NULL,NULL,'1',1,'languagecode'),(1425,1,'LanguageCode','as','Assamese',NULL,NULL,'1',1,'languagecode'),(1426,1,'LanguageCode','av','Avaric',NULL,NULL,'1',1,'languagecode'),(1427,1,'LanguageCode','ay','Aymara',NULL,NULL,'1',1,'languagecode'),(1428,1,'LanguageCode','az','Azerbaijani',NULL,NULL,'1',1,'languagecode'),(1429,1,'LanguageCode','ba','Bashkir',NULL,NULL,'1',1,'languagecode'),(1430,1,'LanguageCode','be','Belarusian',NULL,NULL,'1',1,'languagecode'),(1431,1,'LanguageCode','bg','Bulgarian',NULL,NULL,'1',1,'languagecode'),(1432,1,'LanguageCode','bh','Bihari languages',NULL,NULL,'1',1,'languagecode'),(1433,1,'LanguageCode','bi','Bislama',NULL,NULL,'1',1,'languagecode'),(1434,1,'LanguageCode','bm','Bambara',NULL,NULL,'1',1,'languagecode'),(1435,1,'LanguageCode','bn','Bengali',NULL,NULL,'1',1,'languagecode'),(1436,1,'LanguageCode','bo','Tibetan',NULL,NULL,'1',1,'languagecode'),(1437,1,'LanguageCode','br','Breton',NULL,NULL,'1',1,'languagecode'),(143